## Practical information

CO₂ procedures are available at the Ensana spa hotels in Marienbad; carbonated baths, for example, are among the main procedures at the Centrální Lázně hotel. They form part of comprehensive and contributory spa stays as well as self-paid treatment programmes. For guests insured in the Czech Republic, comprehensive care covers treatment, accommodation and meals, while contributory care covers the treatment only; in both cases the procedures prescribed by the spa physician form part of the covered treatment. Details are in the [guide to spa treatment and insurance](/en/magazine/spa-treatment-insurance-guide).

## Frequently asked questions about CO₂ therapy

### What is "Maria's Gas"?

Maria's Gas is natural carbon dioxide of volcanic origin with a purity of 99.7%, which rises from the Maria Spring in the centre of Marienbad. It is one of the town's four natural healing resources and is used in dry gas baths, carbonated baths and gas injections.

### What happens during a dry gas bath — and does it hurt?

You lie for 20 to 30 minutes in a bag filled with natural CO₂, which is absorbed through the skin. The procedure is painless; most guests feel warmth and a gentle tingling of the skin.

### Which conditions is CO₂ therapy used for?

Above all for diseases of the circulatory system in indication group II — hypertension, arterial disease of the limbs and functional disorders of the peripheral vessels — and, on the basis of spa practice, also for diseases of the musculoskeletal system and in the after-care of chronic wounds. The spa physician decides on inclusion.

### How many procedures are needed?

The number of procedures and their frequency are set by the spa physician; they are usually prescribed several times a week for the whole stay. The length of a covered stay is determined by the item of the Czech indication list — for hypertension II/3, for example, the basic stay is 28 days in comprehensive or 21 days in contributory care.

### Are there contraindications?

Yes. CO₂ procedures are not given, among other cases, for diseases in the acute stage, with signs of circulatory failure, after a recent thrombosis and in pregnancy; gas injections are additionally not given where there is inflammation or a skin disease at the injection site or a clotting disorder. An initial medical examination always takes place before the cure begins.

### Where can I book CO₂ therapy?

At the Ensana spa hotels in Marienbad as part of a treatment stay. All three forms — dry gas baths, carbonated baths and gas injections — are offered by the Ensana Nové Lázně hotel.
